{\*\ftnsep\chftnsep}\pgndec\pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af13\afs28 \ltrch\hich\af7\loch\widctlpar\sb440\sa60\keepn\f7\fs28\b\dbch\af11\ql\sb440\sa60\ltrpar{\loch\lang1036\loch
About Proton-Autogen}
\par \pard\plain \s66\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\sb0\sa140\f4\fs24\dbch\af10\ql\ltrpar{\loch\cs63\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
Proton-Autogen}{\loch
 was born from a simple idea: build the application that I always wanted to have on Linux.}
\par \pard\plain \s66\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\sb0\sa140\f4\fs24\dbch\af10\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Running Windows applications on Linux has become much easier over the years thanks to projects such as Steam, Proton and Wine. However, many existing tools are designed for experienced users, expose a large number of options from the start, or require a good understanding of compatibility layers, prefixes and runtime configuration.}
\par \pard\plain \s66\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\sb0\sa140\f4\fs24\dbch\af10\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Proton-Autogen takes a different approach.}
\par \pard\plain \s66\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\sb0\sa140\f4\fs24\dbch\af10\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Its goal is to make running Windows applications on Linux as simple as launching a native application, while still providing advanced features for users who need them.}
\par \pard\plain \s66\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\sb0\sa140\f4\fs24\dbch\af10\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The philosophy behind the project is straightforward:}
\par \pard\plain \s103\hich\af4\loch\widctlpar\fi0\li567\lin567\ri567\rin567\sb0\sa283\f4\fs24\dbch\af10\ql\ltrpar{\loch\cs63\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
Complex concepts still exist, but users shouldn't have to understand them just to get started.}
\par \pard\plain \s66\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\sb0\sa140\f4\fs24\dbch\af10\ql\ltrpar{\loch
